---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Sports Performance Psychology"
  description="Privacy policy for Sports Performance Psychology: what information we collect, how we use it, cookies, and your rights."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>What information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. Last updated: November 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We collect a minimal amount of information, and only what the site needs to function:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> if you write to us through the contact form, we receive your name, email address, and message so we can reply.</li>
          <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe, we store your email address to send you new articles and updates. You can unsubscribe at any time with the link in any message.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> we may use privacy-friendly analytics tools that collect anonymized usage data (such as pages visited and approximate region) to help us improve the site. This data cannot identify you personally.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>This site uses a small number of cookies to remember basic preferences and to understand aggregate traffic. You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings at any time. See our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p>
        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect to operate the site, respond to your messages, send the newsletter you asked for, and understand which content readers find useful. We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for their marketing.</p>
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>Some parts of the site rely on third-party services (for example, an email provider for the newsletter or an analytics tool). Those services process data according to their own privacy policies, and we choose providers that respect user privacy.</p>
        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We keep contact messages and newsletter subscriptions only as long as needed for the purpose they were collected. If you ask us to delete your information, we will do so unless we are required to keep it for legal reasons.</p>
        <h2>Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you, and to withdraw consent for the newsletter. To exercise any of these rights, write to <a href="mailto:info@sportsperformancepsychology.com">info@sportsperformancepsychology.com</a> and we will respond within a reasonable time.</p>
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy as the site grows. The latest version will always be posted on this page, with the revision date shown above.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
